<title>USA: Neose says gets U.S. patent for genes.</title>
<headline>Neose says gets U.S. patent for genes.</headline>
<dateline>HORSHAM, Pa. 1996-09-26</dateline>
<text>
<p>Neose Technologies Inc said on Wednesday it had been issued a U.S. patent covering bacterial genes that encode enzymes useful for the manufacture of high value carbohydrates.</p>
<p>The patent, covering genes for enzymes called glycosyltransferases, was issued to The Rockefeller University and is licensed exclusively to Neose, the company said.</p>
<p>The enzymes are key to the efficient manufacture of complex carbohydrates, which being developed for a range of nutritional and pharmaceutical uses.  </p>
<p>Neose has entered into an alliance with Abbott Laboratories Inc for the commercialization of breast milk oligosaccharides.</p>
<p>--New York Newsdesk, 212-859-1733</p>
</text>
